WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:11.320
Action. Hi, I'm Rachel. Let's talk about Kimi's slides today.

00:11.320 --> 00:16.240
A presentable slide stack need a clear structure, cohesive design, and often several runs of

00:16.240 --> 00:20.960
editing. Kimi's slides can take care of the entire process, from early research to the

00:20.960 --> 00:26.680
final edits. Give Kimi a topic and it can find relevant data. Dig into the research. It

00:26.680 --> 00:32.400
can then organize everything into a clear and focused story, with a polish of a top consulting

00:32.400 --> 00:37.920
firm. It helps us formatting too. Kimi can turn business data into polish charts,

00:37.920 --> 00:42.520
map project mouse dough onto a timeline, or turn complex relationship into a smart

00:42.520 --> 00:48.520
art. And nothing is locked in place. You can edit the data behind every charts, move

00:48.520 --> 00:53.520
the shape around, and adjust individual notes and connectors in the smart art. You can set

00:53.520 --> 00:58.440
the look and feel from the start. Choose one of Kimi's templates, or upload a PowerPoint,

00:58.440 --> 01:04.160
image, or PDF as reference. Kimi will use the colors and layouts from a reference to keep

01:04.160 --> 01:10.000
the new deck consistent with the brand. Of course, the first draft is really perfect.

01:10.000 --> 01:15.400
You can keep improving it simply by talking to Kimi. Need to change a specific detail?

01:15.400 --> 01:20.560
Leave a comment directly on the slide. Kimi will jump right in and make the change.

01:20.560 --> 01:25.360
The new version history feature takes a record of every draft. If something does not work,

01:25.360 --> 01:31.840
you can simply roll it back. Kimi can also rebuild complex technical diagrams.

01:31.840 --> 01:37.800
Upload an image with PDF, and it can recognize the text, shapes, connectors, and formulas,

01:37.800 --> 01:42.720
and recreate them as elements in PowerPoint can edit. Once you're finished, you can export

01:42.720 --> 01:47.080
your work directly to PowerPoint and keep collaborating with your team. Kimi can also

01:47.080 --> 01:52.880
create posters, infographics, and social media cards. And yes, everything is fully

01:52.880 --> 01:58.640
editable. Open Kimi's slides now, bring your idea to life, and share them with your team.

